y partnership and planning","partnershipIntro":"Shared decisions, lived experience, and relationships that shape better services.","partnershipNoteTitle":"Whose perspective is missing?","partnershipNote":"People affected by a decision may notice barriers that are easy to miss from inside an organization. Their involvement can change both the question and the solution.","partnershipIds":["pn-partnership-spine","ja-stakeholder-map","pn-embed-early","ext-dhs-equity-toolkit","pn-intercultural-method","pn-self-check"],"facilitationTitle":"Learning together","facilitationIntro":"Accessible conversations and learning experiences that carry into everyday practice.","facilitationNoteTitle":"Beyond the session","facilitationNote":"After a lunch and learn, what would help people use an idea in their work? Time to practice and a later conversation can help learning continue.","facilitationIds":["lm-facilitation-application","ja-facilitation-session-plan","ja-access-checks","lm-workplace-climate"]}},{"surfaceId":"amplify.materials","routePattern":"/one-dsd/amplify/materials","staffLabel":"Make it your own","scopePolicy":"dsd","fieldContract":[{"key":"title","label":"title","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":2000},{"key":"intro","label":"intro","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":2000},{"key":"backLabel","label":"backLabel","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":2000},{"key":"resourcesTitle","label":"resourcesTitle","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":2000},{"key":"navigation","label":"Page links","kind":"link-list","required":true},{"key":"resources","label":"Related resources","kind":"link-list"},{"key":"section0Title","label":"An invitation","kind":"short","required":true,"maxLength":200},{"key":"section0Body","label":"An invitation: text","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":4000,"maxItems":30},{"key":"section1Title","label":"A simple opening","kind":"short","required":true,"maxLength":200},{"key":"section1Body","label":"A simple opening: text","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":4000,"maxItems":30},{"key":"section2Title","label":"A 45-minute conversation","kind":"short","required":true,"maxLength":200},{"key":"section2Body","label":"A 45-minute conversation: text","kind":"string-list","required":true,"maxLength":4000,"maxItems":30},{"key":"section3Title","label":"A question to carry forward","kind":"short","required":true,"maxLength":200},{"key":"section3Body","label":"A question to carry forward: text","kind":"string-list","required":true,"maxLength":4000,"maxItems":30},{"key":"section4Title","label":"An update to the group","kind":"short","required":true,"maxLength":200},{"key":"section4Body","label":"An update to the group: text","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":4000,"maxItems":30},{"key":"section5Title","label":"An optional check-in","kind":"short","required":true,"maxLength":200},{"key":"section5Body","label":"An optional check-in: text","kind":"string-list","required":true,"maxLength":4000,"maxItems":30},{"key":"section6Title","label":"Passing the lead","kind":"short","required":true,"maxLength":200},{"key":"section6Body","label":"Passing the lead: text","kind":"string-list","required":true,"maxLength":4000,"maxItems":30},{"key":"section7Title","label":"Before sharing an invitation","kind":"short","required":true,"maxLength":200},{"key":"section7Body","label":"Before sharing an invitation: text","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":4000,"maxItems":30}],"protectedFields":[],"requiredReviewDimensions":["language_alignment","factual_currentness","accessibility","scope","placement"],"approvedValues":{"title":"Make it your own","intro":"Starting points for a welcome, a conversation, and staying in touch. Adapt them to the people gathering with you.","backLabel":"One DSD","navigation":[{"label":"Amplify Equity","href":"/one-dsd/amplify"},{"label":"Ideas for gathering","href":"/one-dsd/amplify/gatherings"},{"label":"For co-leads","href":"/one-dsd/amplify/co-leads"},{"label":"Make it your own","href":"/one-dsd/amplify/materials"}],"resourcesTitle":"Useful companions","resources":[{"label":"Open the Amplify space","href":"https://teams.live.com/l/community/FAAzQ3B2126KM9zcQ"},{"label":"Facilitation and learning together","href":"/learn?theme=facilitation"},{"label":"Workplace culture and well-being","href":"/learn?theme=culture"},{"label":"Intercultural practice","href":"/learn?theme=intercultural"}],"section0Title":"An invitation","section0Body":"You are welcome to join an Amplify Equity conversation. We will explore [topic] on [date and time], at [joining details]. Come to share, listen, or ask a question. Participation is voluntary, and no preparation is needed. Contact [co-lead] with questions or to discuss what would help you participate.","section1Title":"A simple opening","section1Body":"Welcome. There is room to speak, listen, or pass. Please speak from your own experience and leave room for others. We can question ideas without making assumptions about one another. Please keep names and private stories about other people out of the conversation. Today we are exploring [question].","section2Title":"A 45-minute conversation","section2Body":["First 5 minutes: welcome, ways to participate, and the opening question.","Next 10 minutes: a quiet reflection, short reading, or everyday example. No personal disclosure is required.","Next 20 minutes: explore what people notice and what they wonder about. Leave room for different interpretations.","Last 10 minutes: share a takeaway and decide together whether anything needs follow-up. Ending with connection alone is welcome."],"section3Title":"A question to carry forward","section3Body":["The question we agreed to share: [wording].","Why it matters for work, access, or people's experience: [brief explanation without identifying details].","What we are asking for: [information, consideration, or a response].","Where it is going and who has agreed to receive it: [person or group].","Who will bring back an update, and when: [co-lead and agreed date].","What we have permission to share: [agreed boundaries]."],"section4Title":"An update to the group","section4Body":"Last time, we agreed to share [question]. [Person or group] has [responded / agreed to consider it / not yet responded]. What we know so far is [update]. The next agreed step is [step, if any]. We will check back [time]. There is no new assignment for participants unless someone chooses to help.","section5Title":"An optional check-in","section5Body":["What felt worthwhile?","Was there a way to participate that suited you?","What would you change or explore next?","Is there something you would prefer to raise privately through an appropriate workplace contact?"],"section6Title":"Passing the lead","section6Body":["What participants want to continue or change.","Upcoming arrangements that have actually been confirmed.","Shared materials and where to find them.","Questions awaiting a response, their agreed recipients, and the next check-in.","What would make the role manageable for the next co-lead.","Leave out participant profiles, private disclosures, and judgments about people's views."],"section7Title":"Before sharing an invitation","section7Body":"Replace the bracketed details with confirmed information. Choose a contact and joining location that are appropriate for the group. The invitation does not need a long explanation of equity or a promise of outcomes; a clear welcome and an honest description are enough."}},{"surfaceId":"amplify.home","routePattern":"/one-dsd/amplify","staffLabel":"Amplify Equity","scopePolicy":"dsd","fieldContract":[{"key":"title","label":"title","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":2000},{"key":"intro","label":"intro","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":2000},{"key":"backLabel","label":"backLabel","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":2000},{"key":"resourcesTitle","label":"resourcesTitle","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":2000},{"key":"navigation","label":"Page links","kind":"link-list","required":true},{"key":"resources","label":"Related resources","kind":"link-list"},{"key":"section0Title","label":"Come as you are","kind":"short","required":true,"maxLength":200},{"key":"section0Body","label":"Come as you are: text","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":4000,"maxItems":30},{"key":"section1Title","label":"Room for different conversations","kind":"short","required":true,"maxLength":200},{"key":"section1Body","label":"Room for different conversations: text","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":4000,"maxItems":30},{"key":"section2Title","label":"What is on your mind?","kind":"short","required":true,"maxLength":200},{"key":"section2Body","label":"What is on your mind?: text","kind":"string-list","required":true,"maxLength":4000,"maxItems":30},{"key":"section3Title","label":"Staff led and connected","kind":"short","required":true,"maxLength":200},{"key":"section3Body","label":"Staff led and connected: text","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":4000,"maxItems":30},{"key":"section4Title","label":"A conversation can be enough","kind":"short","required":true,"maxLength":200},{"key":"section4Body","label":"A conversation can be enough: text","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":4000,"maxItems":30},{"key":"section5Title","label":"Support when it would help","kind":"short","required":true,"maxLength":200},{"key":"section5Body","label":"Support when it would help: text","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":4000,"maxItems":30},{"key":"section6Title","label":"Gatherings","kind":"short","required":true,"maxLength":200},{"key":"section6Body","label":"Gatherings: text","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":4000,"maxItems":30}],"protectedFields":[],"requiredReviewDimensions":["language_alignment","factual_currentness","accessibility","scope","placement"],"approvedValues":{"title":"Amplify Equity","intro":"A place for DSD colleagues to connect, share perspectives, and explore what makes work more welcoming and fair.","backLabel":"One DSD","navigation":[{"label":"Amplify Equity","href":"/one-dsd/amplify"},{"label":"Ideas for gathering","href":"/one-dsd/amplify/gatherings"},{"label":"For co-leads","href":"/one-dsd/amplify/co-leads"},{"label":"Make it your own","href":"/one-dsd/amplify/materials"}],"resourcesTitle":"Useful companions","resources":[{"label":"Open the Amplify space","href":"https://teams.live.com/l/community/FAAzQ3B2126KM9zcQ"},{"label":"Facilitation and learning together","href":"/learn?theme=facilitation"},{"label":"Workplace culture and well-being","href":"/learn?theme=culture"},{"label":"Intercultural practice","href":"/learn?theme=intercultural"}],"section0Title":"Come as you are","section0Body":"You do not need an equity title or prior experience to take part. Bring a question, an idea, or simply your attention. Conversation, cultural celebration, and learning from one another all belong here.","section1Title":"Room for different conversations","section1Body":"Some gatherings begin with a workplace question. Others grow from a reading, a shared interest, or a cultural observance. Staff shape the conversation. There is no required sequence and no expectation that every gathering produces an assignment.","section2Title":"What is on your mind?","section2Body":["What helps you feel heard at work?","What would you like colleagues from another team to understand?","What makes it easier to ask a question or try something unfamiliar?","What is something worth celebrating or learning about together?"],"section3Title":"Staff led and connected","section3Body":"One or two co-leads organize Amplify with staff input. Their connection with the One DSD Team provides a way to share agreed questions and bring back updates. Amplify remains a voluntary engagement space; the One DSD Team has a separate role in the division’s equity work.","section4Title":"A conversation can be enough","section4Body":"Sometimes connection is the outcome. Sometimes a conversation leads to a useful resource or a question that deserves attention elsewhere. Participants and co-leads can agree on what, if anything, to carry forward.","section5Title":"Support when it would help","section5Body":"Facilitation ideas and practical resources are available here. The Equity and Inclusion Operations Consultant can be invited to weigh in on a question or offer specialized support.","section6Title":"Gatherings","section6Body":"Dates and participation details will appear here when arrangements are confirmed."}},{"surfaceId":"amplify.gatherings","routePattern":"/one-dsd/amplify/gatherings","staffLabel":"Ideas for gathering","scopePolicy":"dsd","fieldContract":[{"key":"title","label":"title","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":2000},{"key":"intro","label":"intro","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":2000},{"key":"backLabel","label":"backLabel","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":2000},{"key":"resourcesTitle","label":"resourcesTitle","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":2000},{"key":"navigation","label":"Page links","kind":"link-list","required":true},{"key":"resources","label":"Related resources","kind":"link-list"},{"key":"section0Title","label":"Open conversation","kind":"short","required":true,"maxLength":200},{"key":"section0Body","label":"Open conversation: text","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":4000,"maxItems":30},{"key":"section1Title","label":"Explore together","kind":"short","required":true,"maxLength":200},{"key":"section1Body","label":"Explore together: text","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":4000,"maxItems":30},{"key":"section2Title","label":"Connect and celebrate","kind":"short","required":true,"maxLength":200},{"key":"section2Body","label":"Connect and celebrate: text","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":4000,"maxItems":30},{"key":"section3Title","label":"Ways of working together","kind":"short","required":true,"maxLength":200},{"key":"section3Body","label":"Ways of working together: text","kind":"string-list","required":true,"maxLength":4000,"maxItems":30},{"key":"section4Title","label":"Everyday access","kind":"short","required":true,"maxLength":200},{"key":"section4Body","label":"Everyday access: text","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":4000,"maxItems":30},{"key":"section5Title","label":"Intent and experience","kind":"short","required":true,"maxLength":200},{"key":"section5Body","label":"Intent and experience: text","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":4000,"maxItems":30},{"key":"section6Title","label":"At the close","kind":"short","required":true,"maxLength":200},{"key":"section6Body","label":"At the close: text","kind":"string-list","required":true,"maxLength":4000,"maxItems":30}],"protectedFields":[],"requiredReviewDimensions":["language_alignment","factual_currentness","accessibility","scope","placement"],"approvedValues":{"title":"Ideas for gathering","intro":"Choose a starting point that fits the people and the moment. Leave room for the conversation to take its own shape.","backLabel":"One DSD","navigation":[{"label":"Amplify Equity","href":"/one-dsd/amplify"},{"label":"Ideas for gathering","href":"/one-dsd/amplify/gatherings"},{"label":"For co-leads","href":"/one-dsd/amplify/co-leads"},{"label":"Make it your own","href":"/one-dsd/amplify/materials"}],"resourcesTitle":"Useful companions","resources":[{"label":"Open the Amplify space","href":"https://teams.live.com/l/community/FAAzQ3B2126KM9zcQ"},{"label":"Facilitation and learning together","href":"/learn?theme=facilitation"},{"label":"Workplace culture and well-being","href":"/learn?theme=culture"},{"label":"Intercultural practice","href":"/learn?theme=intercultural"}],"section0Title":"Open conversation","section0Body":"Begin with a question people can answer from their own experience. Allow a quiet moment before inviting responses. People may speak, listen, or pass.","section1Title":"Explore together","section1Body":"A short reading, a video, or a question can open a conversation. Let people know the topic in advance. No one needs to have completed the reading to belong in the discussion.","section2Title":"Connect and celebrate","section2Body":"A shared interest, cultural observance, creative activity, or story can bring colleagues together. Invite contributions without expecting someone to represent a community or provide personal history.","section3Title":"Ways of working together","section3Body":["What helps you think before you respond?","When is written feedback more useful than a conversation?","What makes a meeting easier to participate in?","What might we change so more people can contribute?"],"section4Title":"Everyday access","section4Body":"Consider a familiar meeting, message, or form. What makes it easy to use? What might someone experience differently? Discuss an example without including private information about a colleague or a person receiving services.","section5Title":"Intent and experience","section5Body":"Think about a practice that was meant to help but worked differently for someone else. What can we learn from both the intention and the experience? There is room to examine a practice without assuming someone’s motives.","section6Title":"At the close","section6Body":["Keep it as a conversation, with no follow-up needed.","Choose a resource or another discussion to explore together.","Agree on a question the co-leads can carry forward."]}},{"surfaceId":"amplify.co-leads","routePattern":"/one-dsd/amplify/co-leads","staffLabel":"For co-leads","scopePolicy":"dsd","fieldContract":[{"key":"title","label":"title","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":2000},{"key":"intro","label":"intro","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":2000},{"key":"backLabel","label":"backLabel","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":2000},{"key":"resourcesTitle","label":"resourcesTitle","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":2000},{"key":"navigation","label":"Page links","kind":"link-list","required":true},{"key":"resources","label":"Related resources","kind":"link-list"},{"key":"section0Title","label":"Share the lead","kind":"short","required":true,"maxLength":200},{"key":"section0Body","label":"Share the lead: text","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":4000,"maxItems":30},{"key":"section1Title","label":"Before a gathering","kind":"short","required":true,"maxLength":200},{"key":"section1Body","label":"Before a gathering: text","kind":"string-list","required":true,"maxLength":4000,"maxItems":30},{"key":"section2Title","label":"Make room","kind":"short","required":true,"maxLength":200},{"key":"section2Body","label":"Make room: text","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":4000,"maxItems":30},{"key":"section3Title","label":"When a conversation becomes difficult","kind":"short","required":true,"maxLength":200},{"key":"section3Body","label":"When a conversation becomes difficult: text","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":4000,"maxItems":30},{"key":"section4Title","label":"Different perspectives","kind":"short","required":true,"maxLength":200},{"key":"section4Body","label":"Different perspectives: text","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":4000,"maxItems":30},{"key":"section5Title","label":"Carry forward by agreement","kind":"short","required":true,"maxLength":200},{"key":"section5Body","label":"Carry forward by agreement: text","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":4000,"maxItems":30},{"key":"section6Title","label":"Close the loop","kind":"short","required":true,"maxLength":200},{"key":"section6Body","label":"Close the loop: text","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":4000,"maxItems":30},{"key":"section7Title","label":"Care with information","kind":"short","required":true,"maxLength":200},{"key":"section7Body","label":"Care with information: text","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":4000,"maxItems":30},{"key":"section8Title","label":"Keep the group worthwhile","kind":"short","required":true,"maxLength":200},{"key":"section8Body","label":"Keep the group worthwhile: text","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":4000,"maxItems":30},{"key":"section9Title","label":"Support without dependence","kind":"short","required":true,"maxLength":200},{"key":"section9Body","label":"Support without dependence: text","kind":"long","required":true,"maxLength":4000,"maxItems":30}],"protectedFields":[],"requiredReviewDimensions":["language_alignment","factual_currentness","accessibility","scope","placement"],"approvedValues":{"title":"For co-leads","intro":"A little preparation gives people room to participate. You do not have to be the expert on every topic.","backLabel":"One DSD","navigation":[{"label":"Amplify Equity","href":"/one-dsd/amplify"},{"label":"Ideas for gathering","href":"/one-dsd/amplify/gatherings"},{"label":"For co-leads","href":"/one-dsd/amplify/co-leads"},{"label":"Make it your own","href":"/one-dsd/amplify/materials"}],"resourcesTitle":"Useful companions","resources":[{"label":"Open the Amplify space","href":"https://teams.live.com/l/community/FAAzQ3B2126KM9zcQ"},{"label":"Facilitation and learning together","href":"/learn?theme=facilitation"},{"label":"Workplace culture and well-being","href":"/learn?theme=culture"},{"label":"Intercultural practice","href":"/learn?theme=intercultural"}],"section0Title":"Share the lead","section0Body":"One or two co-leads organize the group with staff input. Share preparation, invite help, and make stepping back possible. The connection with the One DSD Team supports communication; it does not make co-leads responsible for solving every issue.","section1Title":"Before a gathering","section1Body":["Choose a topic with participants rather than preparing a full lesson.","Share the time, joining details, and an optional opening question.","Consider access needs and offer more than one way to contribute.","Agree who will welcome people and help the conversation stay respectful."],"section2Title":"Make room","section2Body":"Invite different perspectives without requiring personal disclosure. Allow people to listen, pass, or step away. No one is expected to speak for an entire community. Questions and disagreement can belong alongside care for one another.","section3Title":"When a conversation becomes difficult","section3Body":"Pause if people are being targeted or the conversation needs care. Name the specific concern without judging a person’s character. Give people room to clarify or repair. Seek additional support when needed; hosting does not make you an investigator.","section4Title":"Different perspectives","section4Body":"A framework can help people notice something, and it can also be questioned. Ask what practice is being discussed, what supports an interpretation, and what other explanation deserves consideration. Agreement with a particular framework is not a condition of participation.","section5Title":"Carry forward by agreement","section5Body":"Ask whether participants want a question shared beyond the gathering. Agree on the wording and destination. Share only what is needed, without identifiable personal stories. A concern does not have to affect a majority to deserve attention.","section6Title":"Close the loop","section6Body":"Bring back an update when a question has been carried forward, including when a response is still pending. The appropriate person or group takes responsibility for any further work. Raising a concern does not make a participant responsible for resolving it.","section7Title":"Care with information","section7Body":"Do not promise absolute confidentiality. Avoid recording or transcribing gatherings as a routine practice. Explain any relevant limits before sensitive discussion. Keep identifiable workplace concerns and personal assessment results out of shared materials.","section8Title":"Keep the group worthwhile","section8Body":"Occasionally ask what people want more of, what feels unnecessary, and what would make participation easier. Change the format when it no longer fits. Attendance and agreement are not measures of someone’s commitment to equity.","section9Title":"Support without dependence","section9Body":"Use the program’s resources and colleagues’ expertise. Invite the Equity and Inclusion Operations Consultant when a particular question needs that support. Routine planning and hosting remain with the co-leads."}},{"surfaceId":"dsd-team.home","routePattern":"/one-dsd/team","staffLabel":"One DSD Team","scopePolicy":"dsd","fieldContract":[{"key":"title","label":"title","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"intro","label":"intro","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"backLabel","label":"backLabel","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"linksTitle","label":"linksTitle","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"links","label":"Related work","kind":"link-list","required":true},{"key":"heading0","label":"Different experience, shared work","kind":"short","required":true},{"key":"body0","label":"Different experience, shared work: text","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"heading1","label":"Begin with a real question","kind":"short","required":true},{"key":"body1","label":"Begin with a real question: text","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"heading2","label":"Contribute where your experience helps","kind":"short","required":true},{"key":"body2","label":"Contribute where your experience helps: text","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"heading3","label":"Learn, examine, try, and return","kind":"short","required":true},{"key":"body3","label":"Learn, examine, try, and return: text","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"heading4","label":"Know who can decide","kind":"short","required":true},{"key":"body4","label":"Know who can decide: text","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"heading5","label":"Meetings and open hours","kind":"short","required":true},{"key":"body5","label":"Meetings and open hours: text","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"heading6","label":"Stay connected with Amplify Equity","kind":"short","required":true},{"key":"body6","label":"Stay connected with Amplify Equity: text","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"heading7","label":"Make resources fit the work","kind":"short","required":true},{"key":"body7","label":"Make resources fit the work: text","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"heading8","label":"A useful work note","kind":"short","required":true},{"key":"body8","label":"A useful work note: text","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"heading9","label":"Keep the work manageable","kind":"short","required":true},{"key":"body9","label":"Keep the work manageable: text","kind":"long","required":true}],"protectedFields":[],"requiredReviewDimensions":["language_alignment","factual_currentness","accessibility","scope","placement"],"approvedValues":{"title":"One DSD Team","intro":"Colleagues working together to make equity part of everyday decisions, programs, and services.","backLabel":"One DSD","linksTitle":"Connected work","links":[{"label":"Open the team space","href":"https://teams.live.com/l/community/FAAZGnsBn1D-N8ExQ"},{"label":"Learning for your work","href":"/my-work/explore"},{"label":"Learning and resources","href":"/learn"},{"label":"Amplify Equity","href":"/one-dsd/amplify"},{"label":"Practical tools","href":"/practice"}],"heading0":"Different experience, shared work","body0":"The One DSD Team brings colleagues' knowledge of policy, programs, eligibility, and everyday operations into the division's equity work. Members work with the Equity and Inclusion Operations Consultant to identify barriers, examine practices, and develop useful improvements.","heading1":"Begin with a real question","body1":"Choose a decision or practice that matters to staff or people receiving services. Describe what happens now, who experiences it differently, and what the team needs to understand. Use an example without private or identifying information.","heading2":"Contribute where your experience helps","body2":"Members can explain a process, review a resource, question an assumption, try an improvement, or connect the work with colleagues who need to be involved. Agree on a manageable contribution rather than expecting every member to do every task.","heading3":"Learn, examine, try, and return","body3":"Use relevant learning and evidence to examine the question. Develop a small improvement with the responsible people, agree what would indicate progress, and return to what happened. Keep useful changes and revise what did not work. A meeting is part of the work, not its final result.","heading4":"Know who can decide","body4":"The team develops advice and practical contributions. The person responsible for a policy, budget, service, or staffing decision retains that authority. Agree who will receive a recommendation and who can authorize a trial before promising a change.","heading5":"Meetings and open hours","body5":"General meetings bring shared questions, learning, and updates together. Open hours offer room for a specific question or work in progress. Confirmed arrangements belong in the team's collaboration space; members can also contribute between meetings.","heading6":"Stay connected with Amplify Equity","body6":"Amplify offers voluntary conversation, connection, and shared learning. Its co-leads can bring forward questions participants agree to share and return updates. The One DSD Team considers the work that needs further attention without directing Amplify's everyday conversations.","heading7":"Make resources fit the work","body7":"When reviewing a resource, ask whose work it supports, which task it helps with, what is missing, and whether the example reflects practice. A policy analyst, a supervisor, and an eligibility worker may need different ways into the same subject.","heading8":"A useful work note","body8":"Record the question, the practice being examined, relevant evidence, the proposed improvement, and the person responsible for the next decision. Include the next agreed check-in and what changed. Keep personal disclosures and individual case details out of shared notes.","heading9":"Keep the work manageable","body9":"Choose a small number of shared priorities. Make room to decline or renegotiate a contribution. Periodically ask whether the work is useful, whose perspective is missing, and what support members need. Preserve unfinished questions when membership or responsibilities change."}},{"surfaceId":"work-learning.home","routePattern":"/my-work/explore","staffLabel":"Learning for your work","scopePolicy":"inheritable","fieldContract":[{"key":"title","label":"title","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"intro","label":"intro","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"roleLabel","label":"roleLabel","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"taskLabel","label":"taskLabel","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"anyRole","label":"anyRole","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"anyTask","label":"anyTask","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"submit","label":"submit","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"back","label":"back","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"all","label":"all","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"purposeTitle","label":"purposeTitle","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"resultsTitle","label":"resultsTitle","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"empty","label":"empty","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"choice","label":"choice","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"taskNote","label":"taskNote","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"leadershipLabel","label":"leadership: name","kind":"short","required":true},{"key":"leadershipPurpose","label":"leadership: purpose","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"leadershipIds","label":"leadership: resources","kind":"string-list","maxItems":500},{"key":"policyLabel","label":"policy: name","kind":"short","required":true},{"key":"policyPurpose","label":"policy: purpose","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"policyIds","label":"policy: resources","kind":"string-list","maxItems":500},{"key":"serviceLabel","label":"service: name","kind":"short","required":true},{"key":"servicePurpose","label":"service: purpose","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"serviceIds","label":"service: resources","kind":"string-list","maxItems":500},{"key":"managementLabel","label":"management: name","kind":"short","required":true},{"key":"managementPurpose","label":"management: purpose","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"managementIds","label":"management: resources","kind":"string-list","maxItems":500},{"key":"workforceLabel","label":"workforce: name","kind":"short","required":true},{"key":"workforcePurpose","label":"workforce: purpose","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"workforceIds","label":"workforce: resources","kind":"string-list","maxItems":500},{"key":"fiscalLabel","label":"fiscal: name","kind":"short","required":true},{"key":"fiscalPurpose","label":"fiscal: purpose","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"fiscalIds","label":"fiscal: resources","kind":"string-list","maxItems":500},{"key":"dataLabel","label":"data: name","kind":"short","required":true},{"key":"dataPurpose","label":"data: purpose","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"dataIds","label":"data: resources","kind":"string-list","maxItems":500},{"key":"engagementLabel","label":"engagement: name","kind":"short","required":true},{"key":"engagementPurpose","label":"engagement: purpose","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"engagementIds","label":"engagement: resources","kind":"string-list","maxItems":500},{"key":"communicationLabel","label":"communication: name","kind":"short","required":true},{"key":"communicationPurpose","label":"communication: purpose","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"communicationIds","label":"communication: resources","kind":"string-list","maxItems":500},{"key":"equityLabel","label":"equity: name","kind":"short","required":true},{"key":"equityPurpose","label":"equity: purpose","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"equityIds","label":"equity: resources","kind":"string-list","maxItems":500},{"key":"taskreviewLabel","label":"review: task","kind":"short","required":true},{"key":"taskreviewIds","label":"review: resources","kind":"string-list","maxItems":500},{"key":"taskmeetingLabel","label":"meeting: task","kind":"short","required":true},{"key":"taskmeetingIds","label":"meeting: resources","kind":"string-list","maxItems":500},{"key":"taskpartnershipLabel","label":"partnership: task","kind":"short","required":true},{"key":"taskpartnershipIds","label":"partnership: resources","kind":"string-list","maxItems":500},{"key":"taskchangeLabel","label":"change: task","kind":"short","required":true},{"key":"taskchangeIds","label":"change: resources","kind":"string-list","maxItems":500}],"protectedFields":[],"requiredReviewDimensions":["language_alignment","factual_currentness","accessibility","scope","placement"],"approvedValues":{"title":"Learning for your work","intro":"Different responsibilities call for different examples and tools. Explore a starting point that fits what you are doing today.","roleLabel":"Your area of work","taskLabel":"What are you working on?","anyRole":"Explore without choosing a role","anyTask":"Explore this area","submit":"Explore","back":"My Work","all":"All learning and resources","purposeTitle":"A useful starting point","resultsTitle":"Related learning and tools","empty":"There are no published matches for this selection yet. The full learning collection remains available.","choice":"These choices are optional. They do not change your access, and you can explore any area.","taskNote":"The task you choose comes first; related material for your area of work follows.","leadershipLabel":"Executive and division leadership","leadershipPurpose":"Examine the effects of a proposed direction, identify who can act, and plan how to check results.","leadershipIds":["ext-dhs-equity-toolkit","ja-equity-impact-questions","pn-embed-early"],"policyLabel":"Policy and program analysis","policyPurpose":"Examine who benefits from a rule, where it creates burden, and what evidence could support a better alternative.","policyIds":["ext-dhs-equity-toolkit","ja-process-burden","ja-equity-impact-questions"],"serviceLabel":"Eligibility and service delivery","servicePurpose":"Look at the steps people must navigate, communication needs, and opportunities to make access easier.","serviceIds":["ja-process-burden","ja-access-checks","pn-intercultural-method"],"managementLabel":"Supervision and management","managementPurpose":"Connect fair decisions with the conditions that help staff contribute, raise concerns, and do their work well.","managementIds":["lm-workplace-climate","ja-climate-action-plan","ja-access-checks"],"workforceLabel":"Hiring and workforce development","workforcePurpose":"Examine requirements, access to opportunity, and the employee experience beyond the initial hiring decision.","workforceIds":["ext-dhs-equity-toolkit","ja-equity-impact-questions","lm-workplace-climate"],"fiscalLabel":"Budgets, grants, and contracts","fiscalPurpose":"Consider who can meet the requirements, where costs and burdens fall, and how the decision will be reviewed.","fiscalIds":["ja-equity-impact-questions","ja-process-burden","pn-embed-early"],"dataLabel":"Data, research, and quality","dataPurpose":"Define the decision question, examine what the evidence can show, and identify whose experience may be missing.","dataIds":["ja-equity-impact-questions","ja-stakeholder-map","pn-self-check"],"engagementLabel":"Community engagement and partnership","engagementPurpose":"Consider who can influence a decision, what participation requires, and how people will hear what happened next.","engagementIds":["pn-partnership-spine","ja-stakeholder-map","pn-intercultural-method"],"communicationLabel":"Communication and accessibility","communicationPurpose":"Examine whether people can find, understand, and use information in the form they need.","communicationIds":["ja-access-checks","ja-process-burden","pn-intercultural-method"],"equityLabel":"Equity practice and organizational change","equityPurpose":"Connect a specific barrier with the wider process, responsible partners, and a change that can be sustained.","equityIds":["ext-dhs-equity-toolkit","pn-embed-early","ja-launch-embed-checklist"],"taskreviewLabel":"Review a policy or process","taskreviewIds":["ja-process-burden","ext-dhs-equity-toolkit","ja-equity-impact-questions"],"taskmeetingLabel":"Plan a meeting or learning session","taskmeetingIds":["ja-access-checks","ja-facilitation-session-plan","lm-facilitation-application"],"taskpartnershipLabel":"Involve people in a decision","taskpartnershipIds":["ja-stakeholder-map","pn-partnership-spine","pn-intercultural-method"],"taskchangeLabel":"Put an improvement into practice","taskchangeIds":["pn-embed-early","ja-launch-embed-checklist","ja-climate-action-plan"]}},{"surfaceId":"workforce.dhs","routePattern":"/consultant/workforce/dhs","staffLabel":"Work map: Department of Human Services","scopePolicy":"one-dhs","fieldContract":[{"key":"name","label":"Area name","kind":"short","required":true},{"key":"relationship","label":"Organizational relationship","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"status","label":"What has been confirmed","kind":"long","required":true},{"key":"leadership","label":"Leadership and decision responsibilities","kind":"string-list","required":false},{"key":"roles","label":"Working roles and responsibilities","kind":"rich-blocks","required":false,"maxItems":200},{"key":"changes","label":"Changes to retain","kind":"string-list","required":false,"maxItems":200},{"key":"sources","label":"Supporting information","kind":"link-list","required":false},{"key":"resources","label":"Related learning and tools","kind":"link-list","required":false}],"protectedFields":[],"requiredReviewDimensions":["language_alignment","factual_currentness","accessibility","scope","placement"],"approvedValues":{"name":"Department of Human Services","relationship":"Agency-level reference.","status":"Public directory reference checked September 6, 2026. Detailed positions and local responsibilities still need confirmation.","leadership":[],"roles":[{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Human Services Program Specialist 1 — classification 2458"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The specification describes professional support for program implementation, including analysis, research, fiscal review, and administrative work. Suggested learning connection: examine a process, interpret evidence, and communicate findings. Actual duties require position-level confirmation."},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Human Services Program Consultant — classification 3322"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The specification describes complex work across programs involving policy, legislation, services, or compliance. Suggested learning connection: examine cross-program effects, compare policy options, and plan an improvement with responsible partners. This does not identify the owner's classification."},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Human Services Manager 1 — classification 3916"},{"type":"paragraph","text":"The specification describes program management involving priorities, people, resources, and evaluation. Suggested learning connection: examine resource decisions, clarify responsibility, and assess an improvement. A general classification description does not establish an individual's delegated authority."}],"changes":[],"sources":[{"label":"DHS organizational information","href":"https://mn.gov/dhs/about-us/contact-us/agencywide-organization/"},{"label":"Program Specialist 1 specification","href":"https://mn.gov/mmb-stat/hr-toolbox/002-class-and-compensation/001-classification/class-specs/h/2458-hum-serv-prog-spec-1.pdf"},{"label":"Program Consultant specification","href":"https://mn.gov/mmb-stat/hr-toolbox/002-class-and-compensation/001-classification/class-specs/h/3322-hum-serv-prog-consultant.pdf"},{"label":"Manager 1 specification","href":"https://mn.gov/mmb-stat/hr-toolbox/002-class-and-compensation/001-classification/class-specs/h/3916-hum-serv-mgr-1.pdf"}],"resources":[{"label":"Learning fo