before the design is settled.","graduatedLooksLike":"By the end, you will have a completed equity and access checklist for your program, with clear responsibilities and a review date. You can usually complete routine planning without a consultation, use the same approach for future work, and seek another perspective when added judgment would help.","askStarters":["We're planning a new digital application for benefits renewals. What equity questions should we ask before the design is settled?","What access assumptions should I consider while the idea is still taking shape?","Who should be involved before the design is fixed?"],"artifactTitle":"Equity and access planning checklist","needsWork":["A quick answer with no next step","A completed checklist without clear responsibilities or a review date","An equity section added without considering access or burden"],"readyToUse":["The checklist is connected to your program","Access, involvement, and assumptions are addressed","Questions that remain are clearly noted and taken to the right people"],"privacy":"Do not include client names or case IDs, and describe populations only in general terms. Progress is saved in the web browser you are using and is not used to rank anyone.","step0Title":"Explore the first questions","step0Guidance":"Use Ask to consider the equity and access questions that matter before the design is settled. The response will include its sources and any limits.","step0Links":[{"label":"Ask a question","href":"/ask?path=gp-1"}],"step1Title":"Consider community context","step1Guidance":"If the work names Minnesota communities or partners, read the relevant brief. Focus on what to ask, access needs, who to involve, and what not to assume.","step1Links":[{"label":"Explore Minnesota Communities","href":"/minnesota-communities"}],"step2Title":"Choose practical resources","step2Guidance":"Use the launch checklist, the journey and burden questions, and the partner map to work through your idea.","step2Links":[{"label":"Launch equity and access checklist","href":"/library/ja-launch-embed-checklist"},{"label":"Journey and burden questions","href":"/library/ja-process-burden"},{"label":"Partner map","href":"/library/ja-stakeholder-map"}],"step3Title":"Draft your equity and access checklist","step3Guidance":"Complete the checklist for your program. It is saved in the web browser you are using, so please leave out client names and case details.","step3Links":[],"step4Title":"Review your work","step4Guidance":"Confirm who is responsible, the access needs you considered, who was involved, what you chose not to assume, the review date, and any questions that remain.","step4Links":[],"step5Title":"Talk it through with a consultant (optional)","step5Guidance":"A consultation can help with early program ideas, high-stakes decisions, or questions that remain after you use these resources. Your checklist will help fill in the request form.","step5Links":[{"label":"Request a consultation","href":"/support/request?path=gp-1"}],"artifactField0Label":"Program or service name","artifactField0Help":"Use the program or service name, not a client's name.","artifactField1Label":"Who this is for, and who carries the burden if it does not work","artifactField1Help":"Use general terms and consider which communities may be missing from the design process.","artifactField2Label":"Access needs and assumptions","artifactField2Help":"Consider broadband, a printer, English, transportation, daytime availability, an available human alternative, and accessible documents.","artifactField3Label":"Languages and vital documents","artifactField3Help":"Note the languages people may need, which documents need translation and human review, and how an interpreter will be available at first contact.","artifactField4Label":"Steps or barriers you can remove","artifactField4Help":"Consider the number of steps, documents, and trips, along with requirements that may be easy to miss.","artifactField5Label":"Who is involved before the design is settled, and what role they have","artifactField5Help":"Consider the Equity Director, accessibility and language access leads, community partners, and Tribal consultation when applicable.","artifactField6Label":"What you chose not to assume","artifactField6Help":"Note the assumptions you avoided about the people affected.","artifactField7Label":"Who is responsible for each follow-up","artifactField7Help":"Add one line for each follow-up, including the action and the person responsible.","artifactField8Label":"Next review date","artifactField8Help":"Choose a date when you will return to this work.","artifactField9Label":"Questions that remain","artifactField9Help":"Note what you still need to learn and who can help.","reviewRule0Label":"Every follow-up has a named owner","reviewRule0Message":"Please name the person responsible for each follow-up.","reviewRule1Label":"A next review date is set","reviewRule1Message":"Please choose a specific date to review this work again.","reviewRule2Label":"This is connected to your specific work","reviewRule2Message":"Please name the program, notice, session, or team this is for.","reviewRule3Label":"Language, disability, and communication access were considered for this work","reviewRule3Message":"Please note the access checks you completed, including language, disability and communication access, and the effort the process asks of people.","reviewRule4Label":"You named who was involved and the role they had","reviewRule4Message":"Please list who was involved before the design was settled and what role or decision-making authority they had.","reviewRule5Label":"You noted what you chose not to assume","reviewRule5Message":"Please note what you chose not to assume about the people affected."}},{"surfaceId":"graduation-path.gp-2","routePattern":"/practice/gp-2","staffLabel":"Policy, form, or notice change path","scopePolicy":"inheritable","fieldContract":[{"key":"title","label":"Path title","kind":"short","r