d, you will have an engagement plan grounded in the relevant Minnesota Communities briefs, with access needs, partners, and assumptions clearly addressed. Review each relevant brief before completing the plan.","askStarters":["How should we plan a listening session with Somali families in Greater Minnesota without stereotyping?","What does the partnership spine mean for a co-design effort?","Who should be involved in a community engagement plan?"],"artifactTitle":"Engagement plan","needsWork":["General cultural facts with no connection to the work","Applying information about a group to a named person"],"readyToUse":["The plan addresses questions, access, involvement, and assumptions","Differences within the community are recognized","Questions that remain are clearly noted"],"privacy":"Briefs do not describe any one person. Please leave case details out of your notes and seek the appropriate authority before using Nation-specific guidance.","step0Title":"Plan a respectful approach","step0Guidance":"Use Ask to consider how the partnership commitments and anti-profiling practices apply to your work.","step0Links":[{"label":"Ask a question","href":"/ask?path=gp-3"}],"step1Title":"Read the relevant community briefs","step1Guidance":"Open the brief for each community named in the work. Read the overview and the guidance on what to ask, access needs, who to involve, and what not to assume. Note in your plan which briefs you reviewed.","step1Links":[{"label":"Explore Minnesota Communities","href":"/minnesota-communities"}],"step2Title":"Choose practical resources","step2Guidance":"Use the meeting and outreach access checklist, partner map, and language access checklist as needed.","step2Links":[{"label":"Access checks before a meeting or outreach","href":"/library/ja-access-checks"},{"label":"Partner map","href":"/library/ja-stakeholder-map"}],"step3Title":"Draft your engagement plan","step3Guidance":"Include the questions you will ask, access needs, who to involve, what 